                <h2
                    class="vibe-text-3xl sm:vibe-text-4xl vibe-font-bold vibe-text-foreground vibe-mb-4">
                    Everything you need
                </h2>
                <p class="vibe-text-lg vibe-text-muted-foreground vibe-max-w-2xl vibe-mx-auto">
                    Built for modern Blazor development with developer experience in mind
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="vibe-grid vibe-grid-cols-1 md:vibe-grid-cols-2 lg:vibe-grid-cols-3 vibe-gap-6">
                <FeatureCard Icon="components" Title="@($"{DocsCatalog.Components.Count} documented components")"
                    Description="From buttons to data tables, each with a live example page. Pre-release: APIs can still change before the beta." />

                <FeatureCard Icon="copy" Title="Own the source"
                    Description="Copy a component's source into your project and change it like your own code, or reference the library instead." />

                <FeatureCard Icon="palette" Title="Themeable"
                    Description="CSS variables for everything. Light and dark mode with runtime switching." />

                <FeatureCard Icon="terminal" Title="CLI-First"
                    Description="Run 'vibe add button' and the CLI copies the component source into your project." />

                <FeatureCard Icon="code" Title="Typed to your models"
                    Description="Components bind your own types, not strings. Select, Combobox and Input are typed today; the other inputs are on the way." />

                <FeatureCard Icon="accessibility" Title="Accessible"
                    Description="Semantic markup, ARIA state, and keyboard support are covered in the core interactive components." />
            </div>

            <div class="vibe-text-center vibe-mt-10">
